WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.500
Hello everyone.

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:03.320
Welcome to Langfocus.

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:05.060
My name is Paul.

00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:08.380
Today I want to talk about Esperanto.

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:12.240
Recently, I've been studying Esperanto with Duolingo.

00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:14.360
But, what is Esperanto?

00:00:14.980 --> 00:00:17.540
Esperanto is a constructed language.

00:00:17.960 --> 00:00:22.160
That means that Esperanto did not develop naturally.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:23.840
It was created,

00:00:24.140 --> 00:00:29.260
Dr. Zamenhof created the language before 1887.

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:33.600
He wanted to create a simple language that is easy to learn.

00:00:33.600 --> 00:00:38.580
Zamenhof successfully created such a language, and that's quite amazing!

00:00:38.840 --> 00:00:43.540
And Esperanto is very easy to learn, compared to other languages.

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:51.120
The billionaire George Soros' father was an author of Esperanto literature.

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:55.960
And he taught Esperanto to George when he was a child.

00:00:56.280 --> 00:01:00.360
In Esperanto, there are only 16 grammar rules.

00:01:00.740 --> 00:01:02.840
And there are no exceptions.

00:01:03.100 --> 00:01:05.780
All nouns end with the letter "o".

00:01:06.060 --> 00:01:07.520
amiko = friend

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:08.440
tago = day

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:12.080
Adjectives end with the letter "a".

00:01:12.420 --> 00:01:14.200
amika = friendly

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:15.020
taga = daily

00:01:15.280 --> 00:01:18.140
Adverbs end with the letter  "e".

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:19.300
amike = in a friendly way

00:01:19.580 --> 00:01:21.140
tage = on a daily basis

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:24.000
There is NO grammatical gender!

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:28.740
(silently) Yes!

00:01:28.860 --> 00:01:31.440
All verbs are conjugated the same.

00:01:31.440 --> 00:01:32.140
mi lernas = I learn

00:01:32.140 --> 00:01:32.960
mi lernis = I learned

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:34.120
mi lernos = I will learn

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:36.700
And the conditional: mi lernus

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:38.520
ALL verbs are like that.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:41.740
You learn one rule, and then you're finished.

00:01:41.760 --> 00:01:43.440
So you progress rapidly.

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:48.800
There are native speakers of Esperanto.

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:54.860
Some Esperanto speakers speak Esperanto with their babies and kids.

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:58.460
Esperanto was based on European languages.

00:01:58.780 --> 00:02:04.620
The roots of Esperanto vocabulary mostly come from Latin and Romance languages.

00:02:05.140 --> 00:02:08.280
I am an English speaker who knows French,

00:02:08.360 --> 00:02:11.720
so I immediately recognize some Esperanto words.

00:02:11.900 --> 00:02:16.140
There are also some Slavic and Germanic words.

00:02:16.360 --> 00:02:20.400
I think that Europeans can learn Esperanto easily.

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:22.360
And, it's very fun to learn.

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:26.400
But, some people say that the language is too European.

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:30.360
And, it's not so easy to learn for non-Europeans.

00:02:30.640 --> 00:02:35.520
Speaking another language in front of another Esperanto speaker

00:02:35.720 --> 00:02:38.040
is called "crocodiling".

00:02:38.300 --> 00:02:39.840
Don't crocodile!

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:44.520
The problem with Esperanto is that it isn't useful.

00:02:44.520 --> 00:02:47.300
It didn't become the international language.

00:02:47.660 --> 00:02:52.660
There is no city or country where many people speak Esperanto.

00:02:52.660 --> 00:02:56.260
There are approximately 2 million speakers in the world.

00:02:56.800 --> 00:02:59.640
But, they communicate on the Internet,

00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:02.540
or at Esperanto meetings.

00:03:02.780 --> 00:03:05.840
Esperanto is just a hobby language.

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:09.280
Is it a good idea to learn Esperanto?

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:14.300
If you want to learn a language that you can use in the street,

00:03:14.500 --> 00:03:16.740
then it's a bad idea.

00:03:17.000 --> 00:03:21.960
If you love languages and you want to learn Esperanto for interest,

00:03:22.420 --> 00:03:24.280
then it's a good idea.

00:03:24.280 --> 00:03:27.380
And if you want to be more familiar with the Romance languages,

00:03:27.760 --> 00:03:33.160
and other European languages, then learning Esperanto first can help you.

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:38.920
Because after learning Esperanto, you will recognize many words in those languages.

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:43.340
Will I continue to study Esperanto until I'm fluent?

